# A common free light cone with native matter

An orthogonal Wilson regulator gives the fermion and photon the same quadratic
free dispersion while retaining the native mass selector, occupation code and
charge representation. Its changed filled sea raises the raw code energy by
about 9.208 native mass units. An explicit positive complement term restores
a unique active physical finite ground with gap greater than half that mass.
A separate, complete prepared-state experiment has a positive matter/field
response. The construction does not prove an interacting relativistic limit.
See [the proof](PROOF.md) and [exact interval receipt](results.json).

From this directory, using the repository Python environment:

```sh
../../../reverse-engineering-reality/.venv/bin/python -B bridge.py --write
../../../reverse-engineering-reality/.venv/bin/python -B bridge.py
../../../reverse-engineering-reality/.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q test_bridge.py -W error
```
